(6032690, 884051, 103142, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how to vote on this one -- it''s a wonderful shot, but I don''t understand what the missed focus is. You may think that the subject is the girl, but you have the focus exactly where is should be on this shot. Unless you''re saying that the dog''s face is too soft and that it''s nice and sharp on the rear. But I guess that amount of softness doesn''t bother me.<br/> <br/>(not voting right now)</td>', 'I don''t know how to vote on this one -- it''s a wonderful shot, but I don''t understand what the missed focus is. You may think that the subject is the girl, but you have the focus exactly where is should be on this shot. Unless you''re saying that the dog''s face is too soft and that it''s nice and sharp on the rear. But I guess that amount of softness doesn''t bother me. (not voting right now)', '2010-05-30 21:11:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6032691, 884661, 103142, '<td valign="top">This is another shot that I''m having a problem with voting. I think the focus is completely appropriate for the shot. Unless you were saying the missed focus was because of a shallow depth of field and that both the girl and the dandelion should be in focus...<br/> <br/>not voting yet -- still considering.</td>', 'This is another shot that I''m having a problem with voting. I think the focus is completely appropriate for the shot. Unless you were saying the missed focus was because of a shallow depth of field and that both the girl and the dandelion should be in focus... not voting yet -- still considering.', '2010-05-30 21:13:59.000000', NULL, 1),
